The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```
struct xhci_hcd *xhci = hcd_to_xhci(port->rhub->hcd);
```
Reason:
This line accesses `port->rhub` without a NULL check. When `xhci->max_ports` exceeds the number of port registers reported by Supported Protocol capabilities, some ports have no associated roothub (port->rhub is NULL), causing a NULL pointer dereference.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```
if (!port->rhub) {
    seq_printf(s, "0x%08x\n", portli);
    return 0;
}
xhci = hcd_to_xhci(port->rhub->hcd);
```
Reason:
A NULL check on `port->rhub` is added before any dereference. If `port->rhub` is NULL, the function prints the PORTLI value in hex and returns early, avoiding the dereference. The assignment of `xhci` is moved after the check to ensure it only occurs when `port->rhub` is valid.

